# Modal nested overlays — z-index check

Whenever a **modal / dialog** hosts another tool or overlay (Select, Popover, Dropdown, Context Menu, Tooltip, Date/DateTime picker, second Confirm, color picker popover, custom portal UI, Advanced Search nested picker, etc.), **verify stacking before shipping**. Nested content that portals to `document.body` with a lower or default z-index will render **behind** the parent modal and appear “broken” or invisible.

## Project baseline

| Layer | Typical class / value |
|-------|------------------------|
| `Modal` / `ConfirmModal` backdrop+panel | `z-100000` |
| Nested portal content (Select, etc.) | **above** parent — e.g. `z-100010` |

Match existing patterns (`DownloadMethodModal`, `HeadingRemapModal`: `Select.Content` with `z-100010`). Do not invent a lower stack than the parent.

## Checklist (required)

1. Identify the **parent** modal/dialog z-index (or stacking context).
2. For every nested tool that uses **Portal** / fixed / absolute overlay, set content z-index **strictly greater** than the parent.
3. Smoke-check: open the parent modal → open the nested tool → confirm it is **fully visible and clickable** (not clipped under the backdrop).
4. If nesting a second modal/confirm on top of the first, ensure the top layer also stacks above the first.

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — Select portal defaults / low z under Modal (z-100000)
<Select.Portal>
  <Select.Content className="…">…</Select.Content>
</Select.Portal>

// ✅ GOOD — nested overlay above Modal
<Select.Portal>
  <Select.Content className="z-100010 …">…</Select.Content>
</Select.Portal>
```

```text
❌ BAD — ship Popover/Tooltip/DatePicker/color UI inside a modal without checking z-index
❌ BAD — assume Radix/React Aria default portal z beats Modal z-100000
✅ GOOD — explicit z above parent; verify visually with the nested tool open
```

Prefer English in new code comments if Korean Unicode might corrupt.
